                "senderName": "NWS Mount Holly NJ",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued August 26 at 2:31PM EDT until August 28 at 4:00AM EDT by NWS Mount Holly NJ",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of northern Delaware, including the following\narea, New Castle, New Jersey, including the following areas,\nCamden, Gloucester, Hunterdon, Mercer, Middlesex, Morris,\nNorthwestern Burlington, Somerset, Sussex and Western Monmouth,\nand southeast Pennsylvania, including the following areas,\nDelaware, Eastern Chester, Eastern Montgomery, Lower Bucks,\nPhiladelphia, Upper Bucks, Western Chester and Western Montgomery.\n\n* WHEN...From Thursday afternoon through late Thursday night.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding may occur in poor drainage and urban areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Showers and thunderstorms are expected to develop by mid-day\nThursday. Some of these showers and thunderstorms are\nexpected to produce very heavy rainfall. 1-2 inches of rain\ncan be expected with localized amounts of 3-5 inches possible\nin the strongest storms.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be prepared to take action\nshould Flash Flood Warnings be issued.",
                "response": "Prepare",
                "note": null,
